  "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Counties_of_Norway (15 counties from 1 January 2024: Viken, Vestfold og Telemark, and Troms og Finnmark dissolved by the Storting's decision of 14 June 2022; cites regjeringen.no 'Fylkesinndelingen fra 2024', which could not be opened in this session)",
  "https://www.ssb.no/en/befolkning/regioner/statistikk/regionale-inndelingar/artikler/from-parish-to-municipality/municipalities-that-changed-county (Statistics Norway: the municipalities whose county in 2024 differs from 2019: Rømskog, Jevnaker, Lunner, Røyken, Hurum to Akershus; Svelvik to Buskerud; Tjeldsund to Troms; Hornindal to Møre og Romsdal; Halsa to Trøndelag)"
 ],
 "notes": "Built from geoBoundaries ADM2 (Kartverket's municipalities of about 2017 to 2019, 431 shapes, names suffixed ' nor' or ' sme') merged into the 15 counties, not from the ADM1 base of the built-in 2020 to 2023 layout: cutting the three dissolved counties out of ADM1 along municipal lines made the clipping library fail on the coast, and Natural Earth's counties of before 2020 lack the changes of 2020. So the eight counties that go on (Oslo, Rogaland, Møre og Romsdal, Nordland, Innlandet, Agder, Vestland, and Trøndelag) keep their names but their outlines differ very slightly from the day before (same mapping authority, a different generalisation). Each municipality is put in the county of 2020 it lies in (by geoBoundaries ADM1), and those of Viken, Vestfold og Telemark, and Troms og Finnmark by list. The county changes of 2020 that were not undone are respected: Rømskog (in Aurskog-Høland), Jevnaker, Lunner, Røyken, and Hurum (in Asker) are in Akershus; Svelvik (in Drammen) is in Buskerud; Tjeldsund is in Troms; Halsa and Rindal are in Trøndelag and Hornindal in Møre og Romsdal. Six municipality names occur in two counties (Våler, Nes, Os, Sande, Herøy, Bø): the base merges same-named units, so each pair is merged into one county and the other one is carved back into its own county by box. Areas built against official: Østfold 3,939 / 4,004 km²; Akershus 5,855 / 5,894; Buskerud 14,612 / 14,694; Vestfold 2,106 / 2,168; Telemark 15,181 / 15,298; Troms 26,013 / 26,190; Finnmark 48,310 / 48,631. Svalbard and Jan Mayen are not counties and are not in the source. The built file roughly doubles in size (261 KB to 526 KB).",
